From fab249847c2b06e892a2934e09e3b4bc65b466ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mounir IDRASSI <mounir.idrassi@idrix.fr>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:12:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] test/run_tests.pl: avoid quadratic time on long test output

With failure buffering enabled, the ALL callback appends nonempty output
lines that it does not recognize as plans or test results to
$output_buffer. Without an explicit return, that branch returns the
accumulated buffer. TAP::Base::_make_callback() invokes callbacks in list
context, even when TAP::Parser calls it in void context, so the buffer is
copied. Each append then costs time proportional to the output accumulated
so far, making processing quadratic for a growing sequence of such lines.

run_tests.pl merges recipe stderr into the stream it reads. While the
harness copies, a command writing enough stderr can fill that pipe and
block. On Linux, with command stderr restored to this stream and the radix
recipe from before #32395, test_quic_radix took 9.9 seconds without the fix
and 2.3 seconds with it. Setting glibc's mmap threshold to a fixed 128 KiB
increased the former to 85 seconds, while the fixed run took 2.3 seconds.
The command blocked writing stderr while the harness kept a CPU busy,
reproducing the signature reported in #32128. These measurements do not
establish the cause of the historical OpenBSD and macOS stalls.

Return no values from the callback; the parser does not use its result.
V=1 disables failure buffering and avoids this accumulation path.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6-astra
Reviewed-by: Jakub Zelenka <jakub.zelenka@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Nikola Pajkovsky <nikolap@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Merge-date: Tue Oct  6 16:04:01 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33078
(cherry picked from commit ab9decd55becb870eb4bf99171dad6e8b706ac24)
---
 test/run_tests.pl | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/run_tests.pl b/test/run_tests.pl
index 89d7fafb7256..ea19d3069f7a 100644
--- a/test/run_tests.pl
+++ b/test/run_tests.pl
@@ -243,6 +243,11 @@ $eres = eval {
                         $output_buffer .= "\n".$self->as_string;
                     }
                 }
+
+                # TAP::Base calls callbacks in list context, so without this
+                # return, every line appended above would also return a copy
+                # of all of $output_buffer, which takes quadratic time.
+                return;
             }
         }
 
